CORE
JmlKotlinDirect
--function "experiment.JmlKotlinDirect.clamp:(III)I" --jml-source src/main/kotlin/JmlKotlinDirect.kt --unwind 5 -cp target/classes
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR
^.*FAILURE$
--
Regression for JML annotations embedded directly in Kotlin
source. JBMC's --jml-source scans the .kt file for //@
clauses, recognizes Kotlin's `package x` (no semicolon) and
`x: Int` parameter syntax, and binds the JML to the
Kotlin-emitted bytecode method by class+method name.

Demonstrates that authors can attach contracts to the Kotlin
class directly without a separate Java stub. The bytecode
is built by kotlinc; the JML file IS the Kotlin source.

Pre-built target/classes/experiment/JmlKotlinDirect.class
ships with the test (kotlinc is not in the test environment).

When this test passes, three independent improvements are
exercised together:
  1. The instance-method parameter-offset fix (jml-instance-method).
  2. Kotlin-syntax package detection (no trailing semicolon).
  3. Kotlin-syntax parameter parsing (`name: Type` instead of
     Java's `Type name`).
